      "short": "$180^\\circ-x$; $x$; opposite angles in a cyclic quadrilateral are supplementary.",
      "worked": "Let $\\angle ABP=x$.\n$$\\angle ABC=180^\\circ-x$$\n($CBP$ is a straight line.)\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\angle ADC&=180^\\circ-(180^\\circ-x)\\\\\\angle ADC&=x\\end{aligned}$$\n(Opposite angles in a cyclic quadrilateral are supplementary.)\n$$\\therefore\\ \\angle ABP=\\angle ADC.$$",
